    "content": "Use analytics and customer feedback to identify friction and prioritize experiments. Find the biggest gap in the journey Segment conversion rates by device, landing page and traffic source before drawing conclusions. Test the path yourself from arrival to confirmation. Compare analytics with support questions, search terms and usability sessions to understand what visitors could not find. Turn observations into a testable hypothesis If mobile visitors often leave after seeing a quote form, test whether removing fields the sales team never uses helps qualified submissions. Define a primary metric, quality guardrail, and test duration before changing the page. For low traffic, use usability testing and note the limits of before-and-after comparisons. Judge the full outcome Track completed orders or qualified enquiries alongside conversion rate. A shorter form that doubles submissions while reducing qualified leads can make sales less efficient. Document results and watch for changes in traffic mix before rolling the test across the site."
