    "content": "Compare timelines, costs, and how each channel contributes to qualified leads. Match the channel to the buying decision Paid search can help test an offer or reach people quickly while you have budget. Organic search builds discoverable pages over time. Use ads to test commercial demand and SEO to improve the pages and information that customers can find independently. Compare the true costs Budget paid media, management and landing-page work together. For SEO, count content, development, reporting and maintenance. A lower cost per click has little meaning if visitors rarely qualify or purchase. Separate branded searches from campaigns aimed at new prospects. Measure the channels together Give both channels an agreed conversion definition. Use search-term findings to improve service pages and send paid visitors to suitable landing pages. Check for overlap using conversion paths and, when practical, controlled experiments. Avoid crediting the same sale twice."
