    "content": "Use performance metrics to prioritize issues that affect real visitors. Understand the three metrics Largest Contentful Paint measures how quickly the main content appears. Interaction to Next Paint measures responsiveness to interactions. Cumulative Layout Shift tracks unexpected movement. The good thresholds are LCP at or below 2.5 seconds, INP at or below 200 milliseconds, and CLS at or below 0.1 at the 75th percentile. Find the bottleneck by template Use field data to see what real visitors experience, then reproduce issues with lab tools. A slow hero image, blocked main thread or unsized embed can point to different fixes. Check mobile and desktop separately. Verify changes under real use Give images dimensions, reduce unnecessary script work and prioritise the resources the first screen needs. Re-test representative pages and watch field data over time. Measure form completion and usability alongside performance scores."
